From c25e984e17856307b21163819b2f8d9ce9b95c6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xander Burchartz <210020462+xanderburchartz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:50:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] Cross-platform fixes found while porting to iOS

These change behaviour on all platforms. Each is a candidate for a
separate upstream pull request.

- shaders.h SetAttributePointerf: unbind the array/element VBOs before
  glVertexAttribPointer. With a VBO still bound, the client pointer was
  read as an offset into that VBO (wrong vertices or a crash).
- s52plib RenderCARC: take the GLSL path only when not drawing to a wxDC.
  m_useGLSL stays true once GL options were set, but the GLSL path has no
  DC branch.
- chcanv MouseEventProcessObjects: convert m_touchdownPos (physical
  pixels) to logical pixels before comparing with the event position.
  With m_displayScale != 1 (HiDPI) and touch, every tap looked like a
  drag and no route point was added.
- chcanv UpdateShips/UpdateAlerts/UpdateAIS: use GetClientSize() instead
  of a wxClientDC created only to get the size.
- MyFrame constructor: wxDisplay::GetFromWindow can return wxNOT_FOUND;
  use monitor 0 then (OnMove already does this).
- options: translate the distance unit labels at use time; the static
  table is initialised before the catalog is loaded.
- ConsoleCanvasWin: initialise pCDI/m_pitemBoxSizerLeg and ignore show
  events before Create() has finished.
- s57reader/s57chart: when an update cancels a cell (DSID EDTN=0), log
  the reason and show a notification instead of only "Cannot initialize
  ENC file".
- BaseDialog::SetInitialSize: wxDisplay(this) falls back to the primary
  display when the window is on none.
- route_printout: write wide strings to the wostringstream, so non-ASCII
  route names survive with a non-UTF-8 locale.
- Build with wxWidgets 3.3: color_types.h includes wx/colour.h and
  wx/hashmap.h; OCPN_AUIManager compares dock parts by address and calls
  UpdateButtonOnScreen with a button state.

Not built or tested on Windows, Linux or macOS desktop; tested on iOS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
